.TH BIGNUMS 3 "2026-09-25" "BigNums 3" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bignums, BigInt, BigFloat \- dynamically allocated integer and float types
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <bignums.h>

typedef struct {
    uint32_t *limbs;
    size_t size;
    size_t capacity;
    int sign;
} BigInt;

typedef struct {
    BigInt mantissa;
    int32_t exp;
    int sign;
    size_t precision;
} BigFloat;

BigInt integer = BIGINT_INIT;
BigFloat floating = BIGFLOAT_INIT;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Integer limbs are little-endian base 2^32 magnitude digits. The integer value
is sign times the magnitude, with sign +1 or -1. Zero has size zero and sign +1;
nonzero values have a nonzero highest active limb. Maintain size <= capacity.
Inactive limbs are unspecified. There is no fixed limb-count limit.
Float values are sign * mantissa * 2^exp with sign +1 or -1 and signed
32-bit exponent. Float precision is a positive significant-limb count,
independent of capacity; default precision is 1024 limbs. Float mantissas must
remain nonnegative (mantissa.sign == +1); the outer sign carries the float sign.
.SH OWNERSHIP
Initialize every input and destination before use. Each object owns its heap
storage. Copy deep-copies a value and can fail. Swap exchanges ownership.
Zero retains capacity (and float precision); Destroy releases storage.
Do not use structure assignment or memcpy to copy owning objects.
Do not reinitialize live objects without first destroying them.
.SH PRECONDITIONS
Callers must provide valid pointers, initialized objects and canonical mantissas.
Direct limb writes require sufficient reserved capacity and initialized active
limbs. Distinct objects must not share ownership of a limb allocation.
.SH ERRORS
Status operations return 0, -1 for allocation/transform failure, INT_MAX for
size/exponent range, -2 for domain/input errors, or -3 for stream errors.
Numeric outputs remain unchanged on failure. Comparisons, bits and scalar
division/remainders have value-returning contracts; consult their pages.
Scalar integer division truncates toward zero and returns an int64_t remainder
with the dividend's sign, or INT64_MIN on a zero divisor without modification.
.SH ABI
This is ABI 3, SONAME libbignums.so.3. Rebuild and migrate ABI 1 or ABI 2 callers.
The object layout, zero representation, ownership rules, count types and several
return signatures changed. Never substitute this library under an older SONAME.
ABI 3 adds BigInt.sign (also changing BigFloat layout), permits negative integer
results, and changes scalar remainder types and the zero-divisor sentinel.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigIntInit (3),
.BR bigFloatInit (3),
.BR bigFloatSetPrecision (3),
.BR bignums (7)
